            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39821-golang.org/x/net",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-39821 high vulnerability for golang.org/x/net package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error.\n\nThis behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/767220",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39821\nSeverity: high\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nVersion: v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110\nFix Version: 0.55.0\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-39821](https://go.dev/cl/767220)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39821**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | golang.org/x/net  | v0.0.0-20210226172049-e18ecbb05110  | 0.55.0  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-39821](https://go.dev/cl/767220)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
