            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-94439-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-94439 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When an HTTP server handler sends a 2xx response to an HTTP/1 CONNECT request and returns without hijacking the connection, the server improperly continues to read and serve requests from the connection. Since a 2xx response to an HTTP/1 CONNECT converts the connection into a tunnel, the server should not treat the connection as continuing to contain HTTP.\n\nThe impact of this misbehavior is mostly limited to potential request smuggling, where an intermediate proxy considers the data on the connection to be tunneled and the server considers it to be HTTP."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/cl/847311",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-94439\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.9,1.27.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/hello-server\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2026-94439](https://go.dev/cl/847311)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-94439**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.26.9,1.27.2  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/hello-server  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2026-94439](https://go.dev/cl/847311)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9538-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9538 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.10 for Perl allow memory exhaustion via attacker controlled entry size field in tar header.  _read_tar() reads each entry's payload with $handle-\u003eread($$data, $block), where $block is derived from the entry's 12-byte size field in the tar header with no upper bound on that value.  A crafted header declaring a multi-gigabyte size causes Perl to allocate a scalar of that size."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9538",
