            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091-zlib1g",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-85091 high vulnerability for zlib1g package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib 1.2.11 through 1.3.2 contains a heap buffer overflow: after an underlying write() fails, gz_write() returns without resetting strm.next_in, leaving it pointed at the caller's buffer. A later gz* write call then derives a position from the stale pointer and writes past a heap allocation; any write() failure reaches it, including EPIPE on a blocking descriptor, and in versions before 1.3.1.2 the failed write must be followed by a gzclearerr() call."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: high\nPackage: zlib1g\nVersion: 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1\nFix Version: 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091)",
