                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95818-libc6",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95818 low vulnerability for libc6 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A stack-based buffer overflow in the dynamic loader (ld.so) of the GNU C Library (glibc) versions 2.14 through 2.44 allows a local attacker to crash or corrupt the memory of setuid/setgid (AT_SECURE) programs.  When such a program's DT_RPATH or DT_RUNPATH begins with $ORIGIN and is followed by NUL or '/' the loader both reads past the end of the path buffer and writes past the end of a stack-allocated internal buffer. The corrupted loader stack can lead to a loader crash (denial of service) and limited disclosure of process memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95818",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-95818\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libc6\nVersion: 2.41-12+deb13u4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-95818](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95818)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-95818**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libc6  | 2.41-12+deb13u4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-95818](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95818)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc6@2.41-12%2Bdeb13u4?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6"
              }
            },
